[signal arg="spot:none"]
Your Grace, I am your Hand. The realm waits while I show you how it answers to you.
- I know the realm
	[end_timeline]
- Show me
[signal arg="spot:chronicle"]
This is your chronicle. Only what needs you stands here, the gravest first.
One new matter at a time, never more than one each minute and a half. The rest is written in the book of the reign.
Every matter has its answers. The one on the right is the one I would give, and Enter gives it.
Go there takes you to the place. Home brings you back.
[signal arg="spot:armies"]
These are your hosts. Click one, then right-click the ground, and it marches there.
Press A and click, and it falls on any foe it meets on the road.
[signal arg="spot:houses"]
The great houses. Swear one to you and its men fight your wars. A gift or a feast warms a cold lord.
War takes their towns one by one, their seat last. Every house remembers what you do to one of them.
[signal arg="spot:pause"]
Pause whenever you need to think. The realm stops, and your orders still go out.
[signal arg="spot:none"]
Nothing guards a town but its own men and your hosts. When raiders come, answer, or it burns.
The realm is yours, Your Grace.
